Comment: 
// @@@ If the list is initially not empty, then the result is either null and the first element was null before the operation, or the result is equal to the first element before the operation.

Interpretation: For pop(), which removes and returns first element. The spec: If initially not empty, then result is either null (if first element was null) OR result equals the first element before operation. So basically result equals old first element (which could be null). So we can assert: !\old(this.isEmpty()) => (\result == null ? \old(this.getFirst()) == null : \result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))). But need to use observer methods: we have getFirst() returns first element, possibly throws if empty. But we only call when not empty. So we can use \old(this.getFirst()).

Simplify: !\old(this.isEmpty()) => (\result == null ? \old(this.getFirst()) == null : \result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))).

