Interpretation: For pop(), if the list was not empty initially, the result (\result) is either null and the first element before operation was null, OR the result equals the first element before operation.

Essentially: if \old(!this.isEmpty()) then (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || (\result.equals(\old(this.getFirst()))). Since elements may be null, equality should be via Objects.equals maybe, but we can use == for null and .equals for non-null? In examples they used .equals for objects. In earlier spec they used this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i))) . So we can use .equals.

Thus condition: !\old(this.isEmpty()) => ( (\result == null && \old(this.getFirst()) == null) || \result.equals(\old(this.getFirst())) ).

